From 74daa759572ec73c51783a5de6420e2a18a2bf18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@do-not-panic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 14:04:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Let a policy drive a rendered race live

--rl-live HOST:PORT TRACE_OUT [LOG] connects to a policy, takes the
race setup from it as a trace header, and then hands it the same
observation the headless bridge produces once per physics tick,
applying the trace line it answers with. What the policy chose is
written to TRACE_OUT in the trace format, so a live race and a
recorded one can be compared line for line.

The game stays a dumb client: it never learns what an action set is,
because the policy replies with controls rather than an action index.
Reuses the replay path for the race setup, the fixed timestep and the
per-tick logging.

Signed-off-by: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@do-not-panic.com>
---
